    <p class="section-number">01 · Traulsen refrigerator not cooling</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Three root causes our techs diagnose first on Traulsen commercial.</h2>

    <p>A Traulsen commercial refrigerator that won't hold below 41°F usually traces to one of three root causes our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair diagnose first across LA County premium hospitality, hotel banquet, hospital food service, and university dining operations. (1) Condenser fan motor failure year 8 to 12 — even on Traulsen premium build quality, the most common single service item across G-Series, R-Series, and RH-Series. Head pressure climbs, cooling capacity drops, box temperature drifts up. $320 to $580 replacement. (2) Dirty condenser coil — kitchen grease and lint accumulate on the condenser fins. About 20 to 25 percent of Traulsen service calls resolve at the $120 commercial diagnostic with cleaning, no parts charge. (3) Smart-Eye controller diagnostic code on G-Series and newer Traulsen units — code reading identifies specific failure subsystem (defrost timer / temperature sensor / evaporator fan signal / condensing unit) faster than legacy guess-and-check diagnostic. Reduces total service time on first visit.</p>

    <p>Traulsen is the "buy once, cry once" of American commercial refrigeration — premium tier, manufactured in Fort Worth, Texas since 1938. Now part of ITW Food Equipment Group (Illinois Tool Works), with sister brands Hobart (cooking and dishwashing), Vulcan (ranges), Stero, and Baxter. Common across Marriott / Hilton / Hyatt hotel kitchens, hospital food service operations, university dining halls, and military food service contracts where reliability matters more than upfront cost. See the broader <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/brands/traulsen/">Traulsen brand pillar</a> for full lineup context. Lifespan tier: G-Series mid-tier 12 to 15 years inland, R-Series and RH-Series premium 15 to 20 years, RIH hospital-grade 18 to 25+ years institutional.</p>

    <p><strong>$120 commercial diagnostic, applied toward repair.</strong> BHGS Registration #A49573 and EPA 608 Universal certified (#1346255700410), plus R-290 propane certification for Traulsen post-2018 green-refrigerant models. CSLB C-20 HVAC. BBB Accredited Business. 90-day warranty. Same-day across LA, OC, Ventura. Next-day Riverside and San Bernardino. Sister sub-services: <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/walk-in-cooler-not-cooling/">walk-in cooler not cooling</a>, <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/true-refrigerator-not-cooling/">True refrigerator not cooling</a>, <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/beverage-air-refrigerator-not-cooling/">Beverage-Air refrigerator not cooling</a>, <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/not-cooling/">generic commercial refrigeration not cooling</a>. Parent: <a href="/commercial/refrigeration/">commercial refrigeration</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 02 DIAGNOSTIC SEQUENCE -->
<section class="section section-gray">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">02 · Five-step diagnostic on every Traulsen not-cooling call</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Smart-Eye code read first, then cheap-first sequence.</h2>

    <ol class="num-list">
      <li><strong>Box temperature documentation.</strong> Probe at product level (not air space at ceiling) to verify current product temperature against the operator's last log entry. Establishes HACCP CCP exceedance window for California Retail Food Code 41°F compliance.</li>
      <li><strong>Smart-Eye diagnostic code read (G-Series and newer Traulsen).</strong> Controller reports specific fault codes when subsystems drift out of spec. Defrost timer fault, temperature sensor fault, evaporator fan signal, condenser temp out-of-spec each have distinct codes. About 60 percent of Traulsen calls with active fault codes resolve at first visit because the code pinpointed the failure subsystem.</li>
      <li><strong>Visual condenser inspection.</strong> Kitchen grease, dust, lint accumulation on fins. If condenser is the diagnosis, cleaning runs $200 to $280 and resolves the call without parts on 20 to 25 percent of LA Traulsen service visits.</li>
      <li><strong>Condenser fan motor amp draw and rotation.</strong> Multimeter at fan motor terminals against rated spec, visual rotation check. Most common single Traulsen service item across all series. $320 to $580 replacement.</li>
      <li><strong>Door gasket plus door switch verification.</strong> Air infiltration at gasket allows warm humid LA kitchen air into the box. Door switch stuck closed keeps interior light running as heat load.</li>
    </ol>

    <p>Most diagnostics complete in 25 to 40 minutes on-site. Our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair walk operators through the findings with photo documentation before any repair work begins. Sealed-system work on R-290 propane Traulsen models requires both EPA 608 Universal certification (#1346255700410) and R-290 hydrocarbon certification.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- 03 TOP CAUSES FREQUENCY -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <p class="section-number">03 · Top causes by frequency</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Across LA County Traulsen service calls.</h2>

    <p>Across LA County Traulsen commercial refrigerator service calls our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair run — DTLA Marriott and Hilton hotel banquet kitchens with G-Series and R-Series reach-ins, Beverly Hills luxury hospitality with R-Series and RH-Series, hospital food service operations across LA County and Pasadena with RIH hospital-grade, university dining halls at UCLA and USC with full Traulsen kitchens, premium chain restaurants with A-Series pass-through and RBC back-bar — the failure breakdown clusters predictably.</p>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>1. Condenser fan motor failure (25-30% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Most common single Traulsen service item across all series. Year 8 to 12 typical wear curve (extended vs mid-tier 5 to 9 due to premium build quality). Head pressure climbs without fan circulation, cooling capacity drops. $320 to $580 replacement, same-day from truck stock for common shaded-pole motor sizes. Common across G-Series, R-Series, RH-Series, RIH, A-Series.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>2. Dirty condenser coil (20-25% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Restaurant kitchen grease, dust, lint accumulate on condenser fins. Resolves at the $120 commercial diagnostic with cleaning on 20 to 25 percent of Traulsen service calls, no parts charge. Standalone deep cleaning $200 to $280.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>3. Smart-Eye controller diagnostic codes (15-20% of G-Series and newer)</h3>
      <p>Smart-Eye reports specific fault codes when subsystems drift out of spec. Defrost timer fault, temperature sensor drift, evaporator fan signal loss, condenser temp out-of-spec each have distinct codes. Code read identifies failure subsystem faster than legacy diagnostic. About 60 percent of Traulsen calls with active Smart-Eye codes resolve at first visit.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>4. Door gasket year 6-8 (10-15% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Compression set, tearing, magnetic seal failure. Premium Traulsen gaskets last longer than mid-tier (year 6-8 vs year 4-6 mid-tier). Warm air infiltration, defrost cycle overwhelmed. $180 to $340 replacement covering G-Series, R-Series, RH-Series, RIH dimensions stocked on truck.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>5. Defrost timer + evaporator fan motor (8-12% of calls)</h3>
      <p>Defrost timer on -011 freezer variants $280 to $440. Evaporator fan motor year 8 to 12 $320 to $520. Combined these resolve about 10 percent of Traulsen not-cooling calls.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cause-block">
      <h3>6. Compressor failure year 12-15 inland / 10-13 coastal (8-10% of calls)</h3>
      <p>G-Series compressor $1,600 to $2,400 all-in. R-Series premium compressor $1,800 to $2,800. RIH hospital-grade $2,000 to $3,200. RUC undercounter $1,200 to $1,800. Higher pricing reflects ITW Food Equipment parts pipeline plus heavier-duty premium compressor specifications.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

